# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# NOTE: The original SPA fallback rule (/*  /index.html  200) was removed on
# purpose. This site is a multi-page static site (index.html + about/privacy/
# terms/faq/changelog/404 pages), not a single-page app. With the splat rule
# present, Cloudflare Pages serves index.html with HTTP 200 for EVERY unknown
# path, which means the custom 404.html page can never be shown and search
# engines index soft-404 duplicates.
#
# With no redirect rules here, Cloudflare Pages automatically:
#   - serves each real file for its own path (e.g. /privacy.html),
#   - serves 404.html with a proper HTTP 404 status for unknown paths,
#   - serves /index.html for "/" (the default index document).
#
# If you ever want pretty extension-less URLs, you can add rules like:
#   /about     /about.html    200
#   /privacy   /privacy.html  200
#   /terms     /terms.html    200
#   /faq       /faq.html      200
#   /changelog /changelog.html 200
